# Line-ending policy: this repo tracks bytes, not normalised text.
#
# build/astronomy_2027.json is a deterministic artifact whose sha256 is the
# project's build identity. Its bytes are generated by build_2027.py (json.dump
# with indent=2 plus a trailing newline) and the generator's line endings are
# platform-deterministic. Git's core.autocrlf rewriting would store an
# LF-normalised blob and hand back a CRLF file on checkout, so a fresh clone
# would materialise a file whose sha256 is NOT the recorded build hash.
#
# Every path below is therefore pinned to binary: no EOL conversion, no diff
# munging. Repo config also sets core.autocrlf=false locally so that what is
# committed is byte-identical to what is on disk.
* -text -diff

# Keep a readable textual diff for the record documents and source, so the
# "which records changed" review is still possible by eye.
*.md -text diff
*.py -text diff
*.yaml -text diff
*.html -text diff
*.txt -text diff
